2. Requests the Secretary-General to continue to inform the Security Council, and to report to the Council on the implementation of this resolution, including on the humanitarian situation, the use of the crossings, any impediments to the delivery of humanitarian assistance, the impact of the reduction in the number of authorized crossings, and recommendations on how to improve cross-line deliveries and address any resulting humanitarian gaps, within 60 days; and further requests the Secretary-General to provide an oral briefing to the Council within 30 days on the humanitarian situation;
3. Emphasizes that the delivery of humanitarian assistance must be in accordance with the humanitarian principles and in coordination with the relevant parties, including the Syrian authorities and United Nations humanitarian agencies and their implementing partners, and that all parties must ensure unhindered access and that assistance reaches all people in need without discrimination;
