5. Reaffirms that the cross-border mechanism is a temporary measure, and calls for the expansion of cross-line deliveries, including to areas not reached by cross-border operations, and requests the United Nations to intensify efforts to expand cross-line deliveries with the consent of the Syrian authorities and without undue restrictions, in accordance with humanitarian principles and international humanitarian law;
6. Stresses the need to strengthen the monitoring and reporting mechanism to prevent diversion of humanitarian assistance to terrorist groups, and requests the Secretary-General to include in his report information on measures taken in this regard, and that such monitoring and reporting shall be consistent with humanitarian principles and shall not impede or delay the delivery of humanitarian assistance;
7. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

